   342|  {id:'x1',book:'No Blue Sky: Built from Dust',copy:'Three ships. No return plan. 730 days of air, and it\'s already leaking.\n\nNo Blue Sky: Built from Dust isn\'t about saving humanity. It\'s about whether a handful of engineers can improvise a civilization from scratch — before their own life support fails.\n\nBob Mills spent decades designing systems for Fermilab and high-energy physics. This isn\'t fantasy. This is survival engineering on a deadline.\n\n☄️ First contact isn\'t aliens. It\'s rust. Read Book 1 of the No Blue Sky series.\n\n🔗 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#NoBlueSky #BuiltFromDust #MarsColony #HardSciFi #SpaceEngineering #MIFECO #BobMills #MartianSurvival #SciFiBooks #IndieAuthor',graphic_prompt:'Close-up of gloved hand pressing against cracked viewport glass on a Mars habitat'},
   343|  {id:'x2',book:'No Blue Sky: The Oxygen Gamble',copy:'Earth sent a \'Welcome Fleet.\'\n\nMars built everything from scratch — reactors, farms, a constitution. Fifty years of independence.\n\nThen Earth showed up to collect.\n\nNo Blue Sky: The Oxygen Gamble is a political thriller about what happens when the colony outgrows the mother country. No laser battles. Just leverage, loyalty, and the hardest question in civilization: who owns the air you breathe?\n\n☄️ Book 2. The struggle for Martian sovereignty begins.\n\n🔗 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#NoBlueSky #TheOxygenGamble #MartianSovereignty #SpacePolitics #HardSciFi #FirstContactButNotAlien #MIFECO #BobMills #IndieSciFi #BookTwo',graphic_prompt:'A Martian-born teenager stands before a holographic display as Earth ships descend through a bruise-colored sky'},
   344|  {id:'x3',book:'No Blue Sky: Rivers Under Mars',copy:'The signal isn\'t coming from a ship. It\'s coming from the vacuum itself.\n\nNo Blue Sky: Rivers Under Mars turns first contact on its head. What if the first message from beyond isn\'t alien — it\'s the universe realizing someone finally built a receiver sensitive enough to hear it breathing?\n\nA Martian diplomat. A distributed AI. A sub-quantum resonance that doesn\'t obey light-speed. And a pattern that feels less like data and more like a heartbeat.\n\n☄️ Book 3. The silence broke. Are you listening?\n\n🔗 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#NoBlueSky #RiversUnderMars #FirstContact #SubQuantum #AlienSignal #HardSciFi #SpaceMystery #MIFECO #BobMills #SciFiBooks',graphic_prompt:'A bioluminescent waveform display in darkness forming an organic heartbeat-like pattern'},
   345|  {id:'x4',book:'No Blue Sky: The Red Charter',copy:'They didn\'t come to the Moon to explore. They came to stay.\n\nNo Blue Sky: The Red Charter is the origin story of humanity\'s first permanent lunar settlement — told through the systems that made it possible. Power grids. Regolith printers. The first argument over resource allocation that nearly ended the whole project before the first habitat inflated.\n\nNo blue skies. No shortcuts. Just 40 chapters of building a home where nothing was designed to live.\n\n☄️ Book 4. From the ground up.\n\n🔗 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#NoBlueSky #TheRedCharter #MoonBase #LunarColony #Artemis #HardSciFi #SpaceInfrastructure #MIFECO #BobMills #SciFiBooks',graphic_prompt:'A dramatic lunar sunrise over Shackleton Crater with astronaut silhouetted against the glare'},
   346|  {id:'x5',book:'No Blue Sky: The First Martian Nation',copy:'They survived the dust. They won their sovereignty. They heard the signal from the void.\n\nNow they build a telescope that sees the universe in colors no human has ever witnessed.\n\nNo Blue Sky: The First Martian Nation — the final volume. From three ships on a dead world to a civilization that belongs among the stars. This isn\'t an ending. It\'s the first clear view of what comes next.\n\n☄️ Book 5. The series finale. All questions answered. New ones found.\n\n🔗 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#NoBlueSky #TheFirstMartianNation #SeriesFinale #DeepSpaceObservatory #LunarBase #SpaceAstronomy #HardSciFi #MIFECO #BobMills #NoBlueSkySeries',graphic_prompt:'Panoramic view from inside the lunar observatory dome revealing a starfield of impossible depth'},
   347|  {id:'x6',book:'Tomorrow is Still Open',copy:'A six-year-old gets shocked by electricity. Or maybe he doesn\'t. The memory is vivid. The wiring diagram is gone. Fifty years later, he\'s still trying to figure out if it really happened — or if the story he\'s told himself is the only thing that matters.\n\nTomorrow is Still Open is Bob Mills\' memoir of science, failure, love, and the courage to start again. From a Michigan cabin to Fermilab. From divorce to adoption. From cancer to building a company that starts with problems, not technology.\n\nNot a book about the future. A book about the memories that made it.\n\n📖 https://mifeco.io/books',hashtags:'#TomorrowIsStillOpen #BobMills #Memoir #EngineeringLife #StartWithProblems #MIFECO #ScienceAndSoul #BookLaunch #PersonalMemoir #Fermilab',graphic_prompt:'Close-up of a weathered engineering notebook open on a workshop bench with a circuit schematic'}
